Viśvāmitra leaves for northern mountain --- Janaka bestows lavish bride-wealth on couples --- Daśaratha marches home with sons, seers and army --- Ominous birds cry while beasts circle auspiciously --- Vasiṣṭha foretells grave danger yet bids calm --- Wind darkens sky with ash and stuns army senseless --- Axe-bearing Paraśurāma appears blazing like fire --- Seers offer worship and Paraśurāma hails Rāma